  "answer": "Fixed `normalizeText` in `normalize.mjs`.\n\n**Change:** `value.trim().toLowerCase()` → `value.trim().replace(/\\s+/g, ' ').toLowerCase()`\n\n**Why it satisfies the spec:**\n- `trim()` removes leading/trailing JavaScript whitespace (spaces, tabs, line breaks, etc.).\n- `replace(/\\s+/g, ' ')` collapses every nonempty internal run of whitespace into a single ASCII space. Since trimming happens first, no stray leading/trailing space is introduced.\n- `toLowerCase()` lowercases all letters via `String.prototype.toLowerCase()`.\n- Empty/whitespace-only input trims to `''`, and `''.replace(...)` stays `''`.\n- The `typeof value !== 'string'` guard still throws a `TypeError` for non-string input.\n\nThe named export and public tests are unchanged.",
